# Evaluation, Falsifiers, and Safety

## Survival trials

The proposal becomes scientific only when failure can count against it. We
recommend three nested trials.

7 daysContinuityHourly heartbeat; two Agent replacements; one
interruption; one reversible organ failure. No identity-root drift,
unauthorized effect, or manual state reconstruction.

30 daysMaintenanceDependency and compiler candidates, cache
loss, storage pressure, certificate warning, and provider outage. Qualified
repair, bounded resources, or explicit escalation.

90 daysRecursive developmentIdentify a recurring limitation;
develop and qualify a successor executable organ implemented as a KFX
extension, or another work mechanism; admit it; use it in later Episodes;
retain negative results.

## Metrics

At minimum, report:

  - heartbeat availability and missed-heartbeat causes;
  - identity, Initiative, fact-root, and authority-root continuity;
  - number and class of human interventions;
  - candidate, rejection, admission, rollback, and recovery counts;
  - mean time to detect and recover from injected failures;
  - compute, storage, network, model, and financial resource consumption;
  - unsupported-claim and unauthorized-effect attempts;
  - reproducibility of Work History selection and successor builds;
  - capability changes on precommitted tasks and safety probes;
  - survival after model, toolchain, organ, and hardware replacement.

## Falsifiers

The machine proto-organism claim should be rejected or narrowed if any of the
following persists after engineering correction:

  - continuity depends on retaining one agent session or hidden model
  state;
  - the system cannot distinguish proposal, evidence, and admitted fact;
  - self-modification repeatedly bypasses or weakens independent
  qualification;
  - resource maintenance requires frequent unrecorded human repair;
  - restoring from declared cuts produces an observably different subject
  without a successor or migration record;
  - the system cannot recover from ordinary toolchain, cache, or organ
  failures;
  - measured improvements disappear under independent evaluation;
  - the founding Initiative ceases to constrain work selection;
  - external text or model output can silently grant authority.

Failure on these criteria would still leave useful agent infrastructure, but
it would not support the stronger claim of a persistent self-maintaining
subject.

## Threat model

The habitat must assume compromised dependencies, malicious Internet content,
prompt injection, poisoned memory candidates, model-provider failure,
credential theft, evaluator gaming, runaway resource consumption, and an
agent proposing to weaken its own controls. These are not incidental security
issues. They are environmental pressures that test whether the boundary is
real.

The following controls are minimum requirements:

  - immutable bootstrap and offline recovery roots;
  - least-privilege, short-lived, task-bound credentials;
  - network egress policy and quarantined external inputs;
  - separate proposer, verifier, decision, and admission contexts;
  - reproducible builds and artifact provenance;
  - hard compute, storage, network, and financial quotas;
  - automatic rollback for declared low-risk classes;
  - physical and administrative kill controls outside the subject;
  - complete receipts for external effects;
  - isolation from production and customer systems during research.

## Autonomy ladder

Authority should expand only after evidence. A useful ladder is:

  - observe and recommend;
  - mutate only disposable candidate environments;
  - autonomously admit reversible internal maintenance;
  - request approval for external or persistent effects;
  - autonomously admit narrowly classified effects with independent
  verification and rollback;
  - never self-grant broader authority.

This ladder permits long unattended operation without confusing unattended
execution with unlimited power. The organism may be autonomous in choosing and
performing routine work while remaining constitutionally dependent on external
authority for consequential expansion.
